<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Bitcoin</dt><dd>An open monetary network and asset governed by independently verified consensus rules.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Open-Source</dt><dd>A development model in which source code is available under a license that permits inspection, use, modification, and redistribution.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Historical milestone</dt><dd>An event or development that materially changed Bitcoin&#39;s technology, adoption, markets, institutions, or culture.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Block</dt><dd>A valid batch of Bitcoin transactions linked to prior chain history through proof of work.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Mining</dt><dd>The proof-of-work process that orders valid transactions into blocks and competes to extend the Bitcoin chain.</dd></div></dl></section>
